      "content": "but you're still framing it as if the \"benefits\" were just some oversight or side effect, while the \"harm\" was the main thing. isn't it also true that protectionist policies can raise costs for everyone and hurt the very people they try to protect? like, if everything gets more expensive, doesn't that hit working class families hard too? seems like you're kind of ignoring the downsides of NOT having these trade deals.",
